# Entity lists, readings and row actions

A household list often combines temperatures, lights, events and helper values. Keep the compact comparison useful without making every row behave like a switch. The native entity domain and explicit row configuration determine the control, not the icon or the displayed words.

<h2 id="readings">Entity, Glance, Sensor and Statistic</h2>

Entity shows one reported state; Glance compares several concise states; Entities allows mixed rows; Sensor can add history; Statistic presents an aggregation for a stated period. A current sensor reading and a statistical mean are different quantities even when the numbers match. History graph, Statistics graph and Activity have different time/data contracts; use [history and statistics](history-and-statistics.html) rather than assigning them one generic “recent” label.

Use the native formatted state and unit. Keep source names, including duplicate or long names, with area or ID context where needed. Missing, unavailable, assumed, null and zero follow [entity state](entity-state.html#ha-ctrl-001-states). State colour supplements text. Do not use row height or a right-aligned value to hide an uncertainty label.

