<h2 id="domain-rows">Domain rows and grouped actions</h2>

The pinned row dispatcher selects specific controls for climate, covers, dates/times, fans, humidifiers, locks, media, numbers, choices, text, timers, updates and valves. Scene and script rows invoke operations; their activation is not a persistent on/off state. A sensor/event row reports information. A simple-entity row deliberately avoids the domain-specific control. An unrecognised domain falls back to a simple row; do not guess a command.

Toggle rows can represent different semantics: enabling an automation changes whether it runs, while turning on a light requests a device state. Describe the actual action. Preserve native special cases such as water-heater rows using climate presentation in this release; do not rewrite the entity domain to match its renderer.

A header toggle or group action must identify the eligible set. Exclude unsupported targets by the native rules and show unavailable or rejected members separately. A partial result must not claim the whole list changed. See [action results](action-results.html#ha-ctrl-002-states).

