<h2 id="special-rows">Attributes and special rows</h2>

| Row kind | Meaning and required context |
| --- | --- |
| Attribute | Name the parent entity and attribute quantity. An absent attribute is not numeric zero. |
| Button / buttons | Give each action its own target-aware name. Do not stretch a row-wide click over nested controls. |
| Conditional | Retain native condition evaluation and a separate way to reach essential information. |
| Divider / section | Use a quiet structural separator or real heading; no control semantics. |
| Weblink | Name the external destination. Opening a link is not sending a device command. |
| Cast | Identify the actual playback target and supported cast behaviour; treat it as an action, not navigation. |
| Text and legacy call-service | Retain compatibility when reading saved configuration. New examples use current action terminology; do not silently rewrite stored IDs. |

Secondary information must state what it measures: last changed is not observation time; area is not device identity. Attribute units come from their contract, not automatically from the parent state's unit. Link and value text must wrap without covering actions.

