<h2 id="more-info">More info and fallback presentation</h2>

Keep the native More info route discoverable by keyboard and a visible action where the row itself has another purpose. A history plot, attributes, controls and entity settings have separate roles. A domain-specific dialog may be unavailable while basic identity or diagnostics remains useful. Preserve the native read-only fallback, disabled/restored messages and permission checks.

The inventory records all 35 dedicated More info control files plus the dispatcher fallback. This does not promise a unique dialog for every platform or imply that every entity has history. Never fabricate a custom control because the source registry falls back to the default presentation.

<h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance checks</h2>

Use a mixed list containing sensor zero, an absent attribute, a scene, an unavailable light and a long media title. Verify each action against its domain. Test a header action with a rejected member, a simple read-only override, no history, and an unknown domain. Read the list with a screen reader: each value must stay associated with its name, unit and action. Confirm sorting does not move keyboard focus to another entity.

Sources: [Entities card](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/entities/), [Statistic card](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/statistic/), [pinned row dispatcher](https://github.com/home-assistant/frontend/blob/e32bc0696ebefde323f5b791269ad0c57f3f99d9/src/panels/lovelace/create-element/create-row-element.ts), and [pinned More info composition](https://github.com/home-assistant/frontend/blob/e32bc0696ebefde323f5b791269ad0c57f3f99d9/src/dialogs/more-info/ha-more-info-info.ts).

<h2 id="evidence">Implementation and evidence boundary</h2>

This is a reference design specification, not a replacement for native Home Assistant components. The examples use invented records and local draft feedback; they do not call Home Assistant. Mapping a registry entry here establishes a design owner, not proof that every integration, browser or device has been tested. Keep native state formatting, translations, permissions, capabilities and event handling. Theme tokens can change presentation; they cannot supply missing application behaviour.

The [interface coverage inventory](../reference/ha-interface-coverage.json) records the finite source baseline and exact mappings. Recheck native behaviour after frontend changes. Use the [native task acceptance process](native-task-accessibility.html) to record what was actually tested.

Apply the [brand rules](../styles/brand.html), [writing guide](../content/index.html), [layout](../styles/layout.html), [colour roles](../styles/colour.html) and [typography](../styles/typography.html). Structural dividers use the quiet border token; editable boundaries and focus indicators remain distinct. Preserve 16px native control text, visible labels, keyboard access and readable names at 320px. A compact arrangement must not remove a capability explanation or essential recovery route.

